    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nImplement `SupportsEagle3` for `GraniteMoeForCausalLM` and `GraniteMoeSharedForCausalLM` (which also serves `GraniteMoeSWAForCausalLM`), so Granite MoE models can serve as targets for aux-hidden-state speculative decoding (EAGLE3, DFlash, DSpark) and for `extract_hidden_states`. Follow-up to #60855, which did the same for dense `GraniteForCausalLM`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Granite MoE targets (`GraniteMoeForCausalLM`, `GraniteMoeSharedForCausalLM`, `GraniteMoeSWAForCausalLM`) can now attach aux-hidden-state drafters and run `extract_hidden_states`. Previously, engine init rejected them because `supports_eagle3` was absent.\n- The captured hidden states match HF `output_hidden_states` at the requested layers.\n- No behavior change when no aux layers are requested: the models return `hidden_states` exactly as before.\n\n## Validation\n\nHidden states extracted with `method=\"extract_hidden_states\"` and `ExampleHiddenStatesConnector`, compared with HF transformers `output_hidden_states` on the same token ids (3 prompts, up to ~450 tokens, bf16, GB200):\n\n`ibm-granite/granite-3.1-1b-a400m-instruct` (`GraniteMoeForCausalLM`, 24 layers)\n\n| Layer | Tokens | Mean cosine | Min cosine | Rel. error | Max abs diff |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1 | 533 | 0.999943 | 0.999575 | 1.06e-02 | 3.12e-02 |\n| 2 | 533 | 0.999924 | 0.997680 | 1.24e-02 | 3.12e-02 |\n| 12 | 533 | 0.999406 | 0.989650 | 4.57e-03 | 1.60e+01 |\n| 21 | 533 | 0.999151 | 0.978144 | 5.49e-03 | 1.60e+01 |\n| 23 | 533 | 0.999116 | 0.981229 | 6.43e-03 | 1.60e+01 |\n\n`ibm-granite/granite-swash-3b-a600m` (`GraniteMoeSWAForCausalLM`, served by `GraniteMoeSharedForCausalLM`; 28 layers, shared experts, sliding-window layers)\n\n| Layer | Tokens | Mean cosine | Min cosine | Rel. error | Max abs diff |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1 | 483 | 0.999945 | 0.997765 | 1.07e-02 | 9.38e-02 |\n| 2 | 483 | 0.999892 | 0.997899 | 1.48e-02 | 9.38e-02 |\n| 14 | 483 | 0.998695 | 0.978420 | 5.11e-02 | 6.25e-01 |\n| 25 | 483 | 0.999317 | 0.971637 | 3.70e-02 | 2.25e+00 |\n| 27 | 483 | 0.999377 | 0.975209 | 3.57e-02 | 4.00e+00 |\n\n```bash\npytest tests/models/test_initialization.py -k 'GraniteMoeForCausalLM or GraniteMoeSharedForCausalLM or GraniteMoeSWAForCausalLM'  # 3 passed\npytest tests/v1/worker/test_eagle3_aux_hidden_states_pp.py  # 9 passed\npre-commit run --files vllm/model_executor/models/granitemoe.py vllm/model_executor/models/granitemoeshared.py  # passed; mypy skipped locally (Python 3.10 host), left to CI\n```\n\n## Details\n\nSame pattern as #60855. The inner models inherit `EagleModelMixin` and record hidden states with `_maybe_add_hidden_state` in the layer loop. The outer `*ForCausalLM` classes declare `SupportsEagle3`. `granitemoeshared.py` has its own model class and layer loop (it does not reuse `GraniteMoeModel.forward`), so both files need the change. Aux hidden states over pipeline parallelism stay unsupported for these models (`supports_aux_hidden_states_over_pp` is left `False`), as in #60855.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
